+The primary E1 observer is \texttt{received\_observations\_v2}. Each new pose and wrench subscription receipt retains its sample identifier and host monotonic timestamp. The observer constructs supported intervals using pose brackets and zero-order-held force. Gaps longer than 0.2 s remain unobserved. The consumed intervals record their source receipt identifiers, interval bounds, and decision times; repeated reads of the command loop's cached state are not counted as new observations.
+
+Offline reproduction uses those exact consumed intervals and the original receipt records, with no post-stop bracket added to the decision evidence. The archived report confirms agreement of online and offline completion and height-reference fields for all 15 original executions. The 19 October additional R report records the same observer/evaluator versions and online/offline agreement in its five runs. This revision reuses those documented checks and the previously extracted precision data. It does not rerun the evaluator with new thresholds or infer higher-rate samples from the lower-rate CSVs.
