+\section{E3: Image-Based Stain-Area Evaluation}
+\label{sec:e3_image_method}
+E3 evaluates a different outcome: the reduction of visible board-marker ink area on a registered surface. This is a post-hoc analysis revision of stored before/after photographs, as documented in the 23 October image-removal report. Its primary metric is
+\begin{equation}
+ \mathrm{Removal}(\%)=100\,\frac{A_{\mathrm{before}}-A_{\mathrm{after}}}{A_{\mathrm{before}}},
+ \label{eq:e3_removal}
+\end{equation}
+where \(A_{\mathrm{before}}\) and \(A_{\mathrm{after}}\) are segmented target-ink pixel areas in the same surface coordinates and fixed evaluation ROI. This denominator is the initial ink area, not the tool footprint, evaluator band, or full image. Residual ink and spreading within the ROI are included even outside the initial ink mask.
